thinkingLevels.markdownDescription:
Selectable reasoning levels, in display order. Keys are the labels shown in the model picker; values are the request params sent when that level is active. Providers disagree on both values and shape — DeepSeek V4 wants a `thinking` wrapper alongside `reasoning_effort`, Kimi K3 wants `reasoning_effort` bare — so declare yours:
```jsonc
"thinkingLevels": {
  "low":  { "reasoning_effort": "low" },
  "high": { "reasoning_effort": "high" },
  "max":  { "reasoning_effort": "max" }
}
```

moby.mcpServers.markdownDescription:
MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers whose tools Moby exposes to the model. Tools are namespaced `mcp__<server>__<tool>`.

**Read from your user settings only** — servers declared in a workspace's `.vscode/settings.json` are ignored (with a warning in the log), because a configured server's `command` runs on your machine without per-call approval. Each VS Code profile carries its own server list. Only stdio servers are supported.

Example:
```json
"moby.mcpServers": {
  "pharos": { "command": "pharos" }
}
```

moby.modelOptions.markdownDescription:
Per-model reasoning options, keyed by model id. Usually set from the model picker rather than by hand.

`thinking` turns reasoning on or off; `thinkingLevel` grades it. They are separate keys so turning thinking off and back on remembers your level. Valid `thinkingLevel` values are whatever the model declares (`thinkingLevels` in `moby.customModels`, or the built-in registry) — an undeclared value is ignored with a warning rather than sent.
```jsonc
"moby.modelOptions": {
  "deepseek-v4-pro-thinking": { "thinking": "off" },
  "kimi-k3": { "thinkingLevel": "low" }
}
```
Note a model that declares no off-knob (Kimi K3 always reasons) ignores `thinking: "off"`.
